## What Did NOT Work (and why)

- **My "63% of E30 videos were made with no events" claim (2026-07-20)** — WRONG,
  retracted. Artifact of Supabase's default 1000-row cap in my own script: I took the edge
  of the page for the edge of reality. Re-measured with `count: 'exact'` + pagination.
- **My "the feed loses every fifth VGEN failure — SH18 logged 50 of 84" claim
  (2026-07-20)** — WRONG, retracted in `160a9998`'s message + code comment. The 84 was
  never real: 34 of those `jobs` rows were GHOSTS (executions died with a queue reset, a
  hand-run script flipped them FAILED). The feed's 50 was correct; `jobs` was over-reporting.
  Both my errors share one root: I drew a conclusion from the difference of two numbers
  without checking they counted the same thing. Cure both times was a key-join
  (`count:exact`, then match by `job_id`).
- **Original "Step 3 = 22% of VGEN runs never write a terminal event"** — dissolved.
  Matching jobs↔events by `job_id`: the 57 with no terminal event are ALL FAILED with no
  `completed_at` and no `error_message` — a shape `markJobFailed` cannot make. Not a logging
  gap; hand-swept ghosts. Led to the reaper instead.
- **Browser verification of `/factory` via the Chrome extension** — failed: the extension
  cannot open localhost here (`Frame ... showing error page`, 3 attempts). Verified via DB
  recount + the Director's own screenshot instead.
- **`npm install` clean** — fails on a stale peer conflict (`@react-three/drei` wants
  `fiber@^8`, repo has 9). Tree was installed with `--legacy-peer-deps`, which strips
  optionals. Skipped install (deps unchanged in the pull; `next/tsx/esbuild/sharp/vitest`
  all resolve). Documented as a repo gotcha.
- **Provider-hang hypothesis for the ghosts** — ruled out: every fetch in the seedance path
  is wrapped in `fetchWithTimeout` and `pollUntilDone` has an overall deadline. The
  execution doesn't hang; it dies with the queue.

